    "Conflict remediation now installs the new base index atomically while leaving combined/resolved working files unstaged; deferred lock cleanup no longer removes a subsequent writer lock after rename.",
    "Retired Herdr FIFOs and client sockets now require exact owned runtime binding, private metadata and no open descriptors; hashed endpoint identity metadata supports source/staged checks without reading streams. Darwin open-FIFO and escaped-path regressions fixed unsafe lsof assumptions.",
    "Real-provider scratch cleanup exposed stale Git staging after commit-tree/ref CAS. Guarded atomic index reconciliation now runs at commit and verified adoption, preserves foreign staging and worktree bytes, and fsyncs the index directory.",
    "Lost ready workspace now refuses before admission Ensure; no silent hot-path re-creation",
    "Retired startup recovery validates immutable target and adapter but tolerates legitimately archived physical workspace",
    "Scratch authorization precedes live shutdown and offline owned-process recovery",
    "Staged deletion verifies every remaining backed-up file and refuses new/changed content; preview does not falsely report completion",
    "Offline Dolt client telemetry/config now isolated from source and retained backup, preserving strict staged checks"
  ],
  "diagnostics": [
    "A full native run found conflict-remediation staging left at the temporary merge tree; reconciliation now atomically normalizes its own known index to the new base. The subsequent dogfood had passed scratch cleanup before this native fix; final verification reruns both.",
    "Third dogfood completed both tasks and 36 turns with clean indexes, but scratch backup refused retired Herdr FIFOs. Owned runtime IPC handling was implemented and tested before the final rerun; failed evidence retained.",
    "Second dogfood completed both tasks and 36 real turns but correctly refused dirty-index cleanup. Its evidence is retained; production commit-index reconciliation and native crash controls were added before the final suite/rerun.",
    "Initial new crash fixture directly updated the ref without broker retirement evidence and correctly failed adoption. Corrected fixture retains owned effect evidence and materializes the interrupted index state.",
    "Initial dogfood retirement fixtures inherited the latest Normal workflow without adapter binding. Pinned non-executing Local fixtures to their base workflow; initial run evidence retained.",
    "Initial dynamic-review fixture retained an executor linked to a closed pre-restart database; fixture was rehydrated.",
    "Workspace fixture initial failures corrected exact pins, configured integration ref and captured review identity; observations retained.",
    "Existing external typed-intent fixture needed schema endpoint for new freshness checks; locally invalid intent still refuses before network.",
    "A supporting-package invocation omitted short TMPDIR and failed Unix socket length; corrected invocation passed.",
    "Native staged recovery exposed source telemetry writes, corrected in production by external per-invocation tool environment."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Retired runtime IPC cleanup requires lsof descriptor enumeration; missing tooling, ambiguous diagnostics and unsupported escaped/non-ASCII endpoint paths refuse deletion.",
    "A process crash that leaves an unknown Git index.lock or index.lock.lock requires explicit operator inspection/repair; automatic recovery preserves unknown locks and refuses adoption. A SIGKILL regression verifies this refusal.",
    "Adapter installation configures reachable adapter endpoints; it does not install or launch vendor executables. Adapter retirement remains unimplemented.",
    "Review preparation creates a deterministic Git worktree; vendor-specific fleet/build-workspace provisioning remains adapter responsibility.",
